CloudBurrow patch 80 to github.com/goccy/bigquery-emulator v0.8.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1623). Needs googlesqlite patch 0080.

The bug: every request finds its project (withProjectMiddleware), and
FindProject read the rows of the project's datasets, and of their tables,
models and routines, as GoogleSQL. googlesqlite compiles a WHERE
comparison to a Go function call per row, and `datasetID IN
UNNEST(@datasetIDs)` decoded the whole array of the project's dataset IDs
again for each row it visited, so each request cost the number of tables
times the number of datasets: a SELECT 1 took 41 ms (from 5 ms) in a
project of 150 datasets of three tables each, as a run of the compat
suite leaves one, and a streamed insert, which the CloudBurrow front turns
into seven engine requests, 370 ms.

The patch reads the same rows, and the project's, as SQLite SQL
(googlesqlite patch 0019's QueryRawContext, and 0080's DecodeStringArray
for the project's dataset IDs) in FindProject's transaction,
FindAllProjects' and FindDataset's: every row of each table, in its
stored order, the order the GoogleSQL scan visited them in, keeping the
projects' and the datasets' asked for. FindProjectWithConn, which has
only a transaction, reads as before. The regression test holds the two reads to the same
result.

